the ocannl-backend marker vocabulary is exactly OCANNL's backends plus none: true
every accepted backend name reaches the facts its backend's module states: true
every backend OCANNL has states facts consistent with one another: true
a name that is not a backend's is refused, never classified by what it contains: true
and a record breaking any one relation is reported: true
the reader's deprecated aliases are exactly the parse table's entries that are not a backend's own name: true
the reader writes every backend OCANNL has under its own name: true
the reader's emitted-code extension is the one each backend's facts state: true
Generated reads every accepted backend name's artifacts under its backend's own extension: true
Generated refuses a name that is no backend's, whatever it contains: true
control: a name that is no backend has no extension in the reader: true
control: an alias added to the parse table alone breaks the alias agreement: true
control: and so does an alias the reader resolves to another backend: true
control: a reader disagreeing on one backend's extension breaks the agreement: true
control: and so does a backend writing under another extension: true
the compiler's sources are read: true
every backend-name constant in the compiler's sources is a reasoned exemption: true
and every exemption counts what its binding holds: true
control: a decision on a name in an expression is refused: true
control: a decision on a name in a pattern is refused: true
control: a deprecated alias is a name too: true
control: a constant beyond an exemption's count makes it stale: true
control: past the boundary, a name held in a variable is not seen: true
